B.bSA=new A.kA("browse_stickers",'List the stickers you may send, as ready-to-write lines:\n- **No arguments** \u2014 every sticker you can send, with its handle and meaning.\n- **`pack`** \u2014 only the stickers of one pack you can send from, named as the app names it.\n- **`query`** \u2014 only stickers whose meaning contains a word (case-insensitive); use it to find the right reaction.\nEach line is `[sticker] <handle> \u2014 <meaning>`. To send that sticker, write the same line in your final answer, on a line of its own: the app renders the picture, and the reader never sees the tag. Use one only when a picture says it better than words.\nThe handles here are the only valid ones: never invent a handle, and never take one from the transcript \u2014 an older turn may name a sticker you can no longer send.\nEvery result starts with "Page X of Y \xb7 N stickers", so page on while X < Y.',B.bEe,!1,!0,!1,B.i4)
